1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:06,026
Public notices can change.
Documents can disappear.

2
00:00:06,626 --> 00:00:12,444
And after the fact, it can be difficult to
establish which version was actually observed.

3
00:00:13,044 --> 00:00:18,648
Sakshi creates a verifiable record of
document observations, using Arkiv.

4
00:00:20,948 --> 00:00:27,248
Sakshi is an independent witness archive for
public recruitment and examination notices.

5
00:00:27,848 --> 00:00:35,322
It records document observations on-chain, and lets anyone
compare a file against the evidence that was recorded.

6
00:00:39,522 --> 00:00:46,533
This demonstration uses synthetic notices, so we can
reproduce changes and removals consistently.

7
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:51,403
The evidence records themselves are
real Arkiv Tiramisu records.

8
00:00:55,203 --> 00:01:01,213
Sakshi hashes the supplied document on your
device, and checks for a matching observation.

9
00:01:01,813 --> 00:01:05,665
A matching hash identifies
recorded evidence for that file.

10
00:01:06,265 --> 00:01:11,721
A changed hash shows that the files differ, and
a removed notice is reported as removed.

11
00:01:12,321 --> 00:01:19,370
And if no qualifying record is found, Sakshi reports
that limitation, rather than inventing certainty.

12
00:01:25,170 --> 00:01:28,335
Sakshi supports multiple witness identities.

13
00:01:28,935 --> 00:01:33,040
For this notice, both addresses
have matching observations.

14
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:40,081
Excluding witness B leaves one trusted witness.
Excluding both leaves no qualifying observation.

15
00:01:40,681 --> 00:01:48,400
Both addresses are operated by the same team, so they are
distinct identities, not independent organisations.

16
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:56,118
The timeline makes document
changes observable.

17
00:01:56,718 --> 00:02:04,111
It records what was observed, and when, without pretending
that a hash alone establishes intent or authenticity.

18
00:02:09,311 --> 00:02:16,414
The same verification is available from the command line, so
the evidence can be inspected outside the browser.

19
00:02:20,814 --> 00:02:24,201
These observations are
recorded on Arkiv Tiramisu.

20
00:02:24,801 --> 00:02:30,383
The transaction and creator can be inspected
independently of the Sakshi interface.

21
00:02:34,483 --> 00:02:39,646
Sakshi makes document observations
verifiable, and changes traceable.

22
00:02:40,246 --> 00:02:42,924
It gives people evidence they can inspect.
